"text": "Course 1 creates no Azure resource. The rules below apply to the courses that run on Azure, and they still describe the frozen files in extras/azure-lab-vm/ of the kit of course 1. Every resource created by Terraform or by a script of a kit carries a tag that names the course and a chapter=NN tag, where NN is the two-digit chapter number, and 00 for the setup. In Terraform, each resource sets tags = local.tags. A resource type that cannot carry tags (budgets, role assignments, subnets) is preceded in Terraform by a comment that starts with # untaggable: and says why. Clean-up commands end by listing everything still tagged for the course. The shared Azure setup of those courses (subscription, budget, quotas, regions, resource providers, Terraform state) is written once, when the first of them is designed."
